   "harm": "Using Update() when not chaining can mask bugs where a fresh assignment is intended and hurts readability",
   "hash": "3994c8dd7f6b9ec6",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:21:53+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:2079388456",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:2079388456",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "I don't think this is good usage of Update(), since there is no chaining happening here. I would find list initialization more readable and less error-prone",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2024-07-09",
    "by": "ryanofsky",
    "id": "c:2218849345",
    "quote": "Also took suggestions to simplify usage in CompleteChainstateInitialization."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/25665#issuecomment-2079388456"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
